            <div class="step2-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Unique Contribution</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-1.png">
                <p>The Ruler Archetype is one of the three archetypes who desire nothing more but to bring structure to the world, and they do so through the act of control.This structure is the Rulers&rsquo; unique contribution to the world, and also how the Ruler Archetype makes sense of the world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>To the Ruler, life is chaotic and unbearable if there is a lack of control and order.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The Ruler Archetype is the polar opposite to the Outlaw archetype.They do not yearn to bring structure to the world through service as the Caregiver does, nor do they wish to use innovation as the source of structure like the Creator does.To the Ruler, structure requires control and rules - it&rsquo;s the only way to do things.</p>
                <p>True to their beliefs, Rulers are almost always known for leading, creating, defining and upholding the structure in the world.They are the rule makers and cannot tolerate anybody freestyling.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Everything that a Ruler does will be disciplined and orderly.&nbsp;</strong></p>
                <p>Rulers are continually organizing and tying things down to a specific, often fair, and just belief system - or set of sequences that can be followed in an orderly fashion.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s safe to say that the Ruler is committed to a fault to their plight. However, as admirable and dedicated as that might sound it doesn&rsquo;t always serve them well - as we will come to see.</p>
                <p>There&rsquo;s not too much in the way that we live our life that the Ruler won&rsquo;t like to try to create order out of.&nbsp;</p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step1-back hover prev f-left">1. Introduction</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
