            <div class="step3-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Sense of Significance</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/sun-glow.png" style="filter:none">
                <p>Attaining a sense of significance is a vital need for everybody.If we don&rsquo;t figure out a way to feel significant, we can start to become stagnant, we might develop poor confidence, and our wellbeing begins to deplete.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Most people naturally figure out a way to develop their sense of significance, and in the case of The Ruler Archetype, they are likely to easily attain a sense of significance - as long as they are in charge of something, which is fairly easy to do.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>The Need for Control and Order</strong></p>
                <p>If a Ruler does not feel in control and has no sense of order in their life things can get ugly.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>They won&rsquo;t stand by and feel insignificant for very long, instead, they&rsquo;ll either turn in on themselves by taking control of something to do with their health or personal care (such as over-exercising) or they&rsquo;ll be tough on themselves which will send them on a downward spiral to depression.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If they are not in control and don&rsquo;t turn in on themselves, it&rsquo;s time to run, because they&rsquo;ll come down on those around them like a ton of bricks and it won&rsquo;t always be nice or fair.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The good news is that it takes a lot for the Ruler to get to this place, most Rulers (because of their sense of fairness) will usually turn on themselves before they turn on others unless they have been brought up to feel immensely insignificant since childhood.And in that situation, they&rsquo;ll be likely to attain their sense of significance unfairly.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Whatever happens, it&rsquo;s rare to find a Ruler who does not manage to find a sense of significance and contribution. It&rsquo;s just that how they go about it in some situations might not be beneficial to themselves or others.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s a fine line that some Rulers will need to walk and learn to master.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Some Rulers Keep on Needing More And More</strong></p>
                <p>Sometimes, just a sense of significance is not enough for a Ruler though. They might want to feel as though they&rsquo;ve made a difference in the world and keep pushing themselves to create bigger and better things.In other words, they might be at the top of their game, but now it&rsquo;s not enough, they need the next thing, the next big hit.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s this challenge that most Rulers have to face because there&rsquo;s always something to conquer and it&rsquo;s difficult for the Ruler to feel completely satisfied they still want more.</p>
                <p>In other situations, the Ruler might damage their sense of significance by finding the responsibility of being highly accountable overwhelming. If they feel that their rules and order are not serving their people or target well enough, this can cause the Ruler to feel inadequate and will damage their sense of significance.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>For most archetypes, just attaining a sense of significance is enough.For others, it&rsquo;s a tough challenge even to achieve any sense of significance at all.But the Ruler has unlimited levels of significance but with such a strong sense of significance comes high levels of responsibility - it&rsquo;s an eternally arduous experience.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Rulers have so much power to bring into the world if only they would learn to lighten up on themselves, give themselves a break sometimes and learn when to stop then they might have some fun in life too.</p>
