            <div class="step4-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Personality Traits</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/floral.png">
                <p><strong>Dominant</strong></p>
                <p>Rulers are one of the most dominant archetypes.They often rise to the top of whatever they do because they are natural leaders and that&rsquo;s exactly how they like it - for they need power and a sense of being in control.</p>
                <p><strong>Brave</strong></p>
                <p>Rulers are brave and fearless, at least they seem to be that way to those around them and are often also inspiring in their approach.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Fair &amp; Charismatic</strong></p>
                <p>At their best, Rulers will lead with a sense of fairness and balance that most people will be able to appreciate and work with.They are often popular and charismatic too.</p>
                <p><strong>Organizes Everything</strong></p>
                <p>The Ruler's primary focus is usually on achieving or maintaining control over something.Which means that if they don&rsquo;t have work to distract their need for control and structure, you can be sure that they&rsquo;ll be exercising this need in the home or through their personal goals or hobbies.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Rulers Call the Shots</strong></p>
                <p>Rulers are usually the people who call the shots, lead the way and get the ball rolling when it comes to organizing social gatherings.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Oppressive</strong></p>
                <p>Of course, there are occasions when the Ruler, may feel out of control in their life and during these times they might display some of the more undesirable character traits of somebody who likes to stay in control such as, poor judgment, oppression, criticism and being overly controlling or oppressive.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>These character traits are the complete opposite of how the Ruler is at their best.Where the Ruler at their best is a pleasure to be around, the Ruler at their worst is someone that even the most forgiving will want to avoid.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Rulers only tend to display this harsher side if the Ruler&rsquo;s sense of self is challenged in some way, and if they don&rsquo;t feel in control - and we reveal more about this later in this report.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Incidentally, learning about the process of individuation is the perfect way for Rulers to protect themselves from feeling out of control since it helps them to understand what&rsquo;s happening to them from an unconscious perspective (and puts them in control!).&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Why Do We Hide Ourselves Even From Ourselves?</strong></p>
                <p>Every person has a hidden side.Jung calls it a shadow aspect, and it&rsquo;s discussed in great detail in our Premium Archetype Reports.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Here at Individuologist.com we realize that there is a hidden side or an unconscious world (to be more precise) that we experience internally, but we don&rsquo;t, or can't show or express this existence outwardly.It&rsquo;s this hidden aspect that can bring about great reward if we were to focus our attention on it. It&rsquo;s also crucial for helping each different archetype overcome their greatest challenge.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Before we get started, it&rsquo;s important to acknowledge that there&rsquo;s also a hidden part of us that remains unconscious even to ourselves too and the process of individuation can help us to uncover these hidden aspects of our &lsquo;self&rsquo; too.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>When we start to uncover these &lsquo;hidden&rsquo; aspects of our &lsquo;self,&rsquo; we begin to learn about what is really driving us.We discover the reasons why we do the things we do (or don&rsquo;t do the things that we want to do, or should do).This gives us the opportunity to start to consciously reconcile these hidden aspects so that we can achieve our deepest desires, or reach our fullest potential.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The Ruler can be diverse in the hidden aspects they keep to themselves and from themselves. These aspects generally depend on the life experiences a Ruler has had as they grew up and upon their unique perspective on the world which can usually be a positive or negative perspective.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>From A Positive Outlook</strong></p>
                <p>If a Ruler has a positive perspective on the way that they view and experience the world, you can expect them sometimes to be afraid of letting people down by losing control and sometimes feeling overwhelmed by the pressure of the responsibilities and dependency they&rsquo;ve created for themselves.</p>
                <p>Rulers might also be afraid of making the wrong decision. Even though this won&rsquo;t stop them from making decisions, they&rsquo;ll carefully weigh up the consequences of being wrong. But they&rsquo;ll probably never tell anyone about this, for it will show that they have doubt and creating doubt in their abilities wouldn&rsquo;t be good leadership!&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>From A Negative Outlook</strong></p>
                <p>Rulers who have a more pessimistic approach to life, or who have had difficulties in their earlier life that has made them feel out of control in their psyche, might become oppressive leaders.And in some cases, the Ruler might secretly enjoy the power they achieve by being this way.Even though at some point a Ruler might regret such decisions and could feel immense guilt over enjoying this tendency they have.It can be like a guilty dark pleasure that some Rulers will enjoy.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If you are a Ruler and you can relate to this description, it is easy to rectify. You just need to start taking a look inside of yourself and learn what parts of your &lsquo;self&rsquo; are feeling out of control. This will allow for reconciliation and turn it into a holistically positive experience even for yourself.</p>
                <p><strong>Rulers Often Sabotage Their Health</strong></p>
                <p>All Rulers will secretly sabotage their health and wellbeing, and even relationships in the pursuit of leadership.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Leading is time-consuming and needs constant attention &ndash; which means that Rulers tend not to relax very easily. They frequently overwork and often consume unhealthy food choices.They may know that they need to change this, but they can&rsquo;t bear to take themselves away from their responsibilities and obligations.</p>
                <p>The premium archetype reports will help with all aspects of a Rulers hidden world. It will help them positively build greater power so that the Ruler can feel stronger internally. It will also help the Ruler to handle the responsibility they create for themselves and alleviate the guilt they might feel if they have chosen to use their power in a way that doesn&rsquo;t serve others very well.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It is your destiny as a Ruler to feel the sense of accomplishment that real power and structure can bring.But to attain this experience, you must first overcome the hurdles that are preventing you from getting there, or that stop you from enjoying your power.&nbsp;</p>
