            <div class="step5-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Strengths</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-2.png">
                <p><strong>Empathetic</strong></p>
                <p>Rulers are generally empathetic, allowing them to often understand the plights of their people.</p>
                <p>They will usually take into consideration the needs of the masses so that they can create and implement long-lasting and successful solutions that solve problems, ensuring that they stay in power.</p>
                <p><strong>Responsible</strong></p>
                <p>As you’d expect with a leader, they are incredibly responsible, and the Ruler is no exception to this.</p>
                <p>Even if the Ruler presents a more negative approach to ruling, they will remain incredibly responsible.  You can rely on Rulers to be consistent and not let you down with whatever mission they are focused on, and you’ll know what purpose they are focused on because they’ll be responsible enough to communicate that to you as we said before Rulers are good leaders - for better or for worse!</p>
                <p><strong>Conscious of their words and actions</strong></p>
                <p>Rulers will pay attention to the final details of whatever it is they rule over.  They’ll be fully aware of their words, actions, and even their body language.  They know that their subliminal messages make all the difference in how others perceive them. And so, they use everything they’ve got to convey trust in upholding power, aligning people to their own objectives through words and actions. </p>
                <p><strong>Can Easily Turn Chaos Into Order</strong></p>
                <p>If you’ve got a problem, you only need to get a Ruler focused on the issue. They’ll have it sorted out in no time at all, making rulers as naturally successful businesspersons.  They can take chaos and turn it into order, just as how a King can quickly draw the sword.  Often, they promote confidence during times of change to the people who are important and likely to stay around after the changes have been made.</p>
                <p>There is nothing that a Ruler can’t apply logic to, even if it means hiring experts to get a problem fixed that the Ruler doesn’t have the skillset to fix.  Rulers know that they don’t have all the answers or the skillset to fix everything, but they’ll be sure to have some contacts they can call on who do.</p>
                <p><strong>Make Excellent Leaders</strong></p>
                <p>Because Rulers are responsible, resourceful and usually empathetic, they make excellent leaders.</p>
                <p>They know that they need to listen to those around them and find a way to address their needs.</p>
                <p>Rulers are also usually charismatic and inspiring which means that they can bring the best out of people. They do this because they know this is a better way to lead and attain co-operation and therefore power.</p>
                
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Weaknesses</h2>
                <p><strong>Crave Power and Responsibility</strong></p>
                <p>Rulers crave power and responsibility a little too much, and they always tend to take on too much too.</p>
                <p>This means that they often get very little spare time to enjoy life as they can never stop, always seeking more and more.  Once they have achieved their goals, they’ll become bored and start to seek out the next challenging project to give them the power kick that they’ve become accustomed too.</p>
                <p>It’s a never-ending circle that doesn’t help the Ruler and can sometimes cause them to make mistakes and can cause them to burn out.</p>
                <p><strong>Compromise Their Health</strong></p>
                <p>As we’ve already mentioned, Rulers tend to take on too much, they don’t know when to stop, and they take their obligations seriously.  It’s just a shame that they don’t take their health as seriously as they do their rise to power.</p>
                <p>It’s not unusual for a Ruler to be powerful in position but weak in body.</p>
                <p>It’s a contradiction that ultimately weakens the Rulers rule, but one that he or she frequently ignores nonetheless.  Rulers need to learn that without their health their power is greatly compromised, maybe looking at it that way will inspire the Ruler to take control of that weakness so that it doesn’t jeopardize their plans in the future. </p>
                <p><strong>Sometimes Too Authoritarian</strong></p>
                <p>Even if a Ruler means well and is not trying to overpower people for their personal gain, they can sometimes become too authoritarian.  They don’t tend to realize or pay attention to the idea that there are times when they need to take off their Rulers hat (such as in their intimate relationships with their partners and with their friends and children).</p>
                <p>This tendency to rule relationships can lead to challenges at home for the Ruler, and even in their work if they haven’t learned to soften their approach.</p>
                <p><strong>Can Find Relationships A Challenge</strong></p>
                <p>Because the Ruler is so dedicated to their mission, which is to bring structure to the world through control, you can imagine that they are probably not the most romantic of archetypes.</p>
                <p>They can often be mentally and emotionally absent because their priorities are elsewhere. Even when the Ruler is the company of their lover they’ll have to work hard to stay present mentally and emotionally, (and not secretly work on their missions mentally).</p>
                <p>Rulers will also have to work hard not to make their relationship another project that they seek to rule.  It’s a tough concept for a Ruler to grasp, but relationships are generally better off when they are 50/50 — something that won’t be easy for a Ruler to do.</p>
