            <div class="step6-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Greatest Challenge</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/success.png">
                <p>The problem for a Ruler is learning how to attain balance.The balance between ruling and relaxing, and also in some cases learning to balance their ego with their conscience.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Some Rulers, although not all of them can become egotistical in their desire for power, but when they push for power and control from an egotistical perspective, problems will arise.The influence of the ego can cause the Ruler to potentially lose control which is the worst thing that could happen to a Ruler.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Instead, if a Ruler can manage their ego, and learn to work for power and control for the greater good (as many will have managed to do), then they have the scope to be incredible leaders if &hellip;</p>
                <p>&hellip; and this leads us onto another of the Rulers greatest challenges and one that will influence all Rulers</p>
                <p>If the Ruler can find a balance between ruling and relaxing.All too often a Ruler will drive themselves to the point of burnout. They&rsquo;ll potentially ruin their relationships, friendships and sense of joy all for the sake of maintaining control and being there for those they lead.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This way of living life is unbalanced and unhealthy, and as we&rsquo;ve already discussed, it&rsquo;s not easy to make good decisions when you are unwell, or not in your right mind.Unfortunately, Rulers fall prey to this problem all of the time.Burnout and exhaustion are real problems for a Ruler, which is compounded by the fact that if a Ruler burns out or becomes sick, they lose control and all sense of significance in a heartbeat.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Unfortunately, though, Rulers don&rsquo;t tend to pay too much attention to their health until it starts to prevent them from doing what they plan to do.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Rulers know prevention is better than cure, and so they should know that now is the perfect time to start paying attention to their health so that they can stay in their power for longer.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Rulers Need To Relax</strong></p>
                <p>Rulers also find it difficult to relax and enjoy life. They may also find it difficult to appreciate and gain joy from the people close to them which can make their relationships challenged and fraught - also not conducive to feeling in control.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If the Ruler could learn how to temper their need to control and take time out to enjoy their loved ones, they would be back in the driving seat of their life in no time. But mastering the art of relaxation and knowing when to stop is a grave challenge for a Ruler.</p>
                <p>If you are a Ruler, don&rsquo;t stay in control of your projects at the prospect of losing control of your health or those important to you.Take time to look at why you don&rsquo;t always prioritize these aspects of your life and start to take the measures you need to take to sort it out. If you have to make it a secret project to work towards that&rsquo;s not a such a bad thing as long as you intentionally focus on those you love without slipping off into concentrating on one of your work-related projects.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The Premium archetype reports will help you to discover more about your &lsquo;self&rsquo; so that you can start to apply some structure to these ideas and also understand why you don&rsquo;t prioritize them as much as you should.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>How The Ruler Archetype can Master their Greatest Challenge</strong></p>
                <p>To overcome their greatest challenge the Ruler needs to look at how they live their life so that they can determine what needs their attention, and what changes they need to make before they lose control of some of the things that are most important to them.</p>
                <p>Rulers need to learn how to relax and have fun so that they can maintain their health and relationships. They also need to learn how to relate to those who are close to them in a way that is equal and without power.Both of these situations are something that Rulers tend to take for granted but would fall apart and lose control of their life without them which is not at all what a Ruler would want for themselves.</p>
                <p><strong>So, in essence, the Ruler risks that which he needs the most.&nbsp;</strong></p>
                <p>Just realizing this is enough for many Rulers to start to ring the changes they need to bring in to counter this problem. But if they are finding it difficult, or still cannot see why they are so vulnerable then the process of individuation is a wonderful tool that will significantly help the Ruler to start to focus their need for control in all the right places.And to permit themselves to take the actions that they need to make to bring in the sense of control that doesn&rsquo;t leave them extremely vulnerable.</p>
                <p>Shadow work, in particular, is an integral part of this process and you can learn more about this in the Premium Archetype Reports.</p>
                <p></p>
